17 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Flowchart compares traditional and AI-driven workflows for IVF across four phases: Pre-Treatment, Laboratory, Transfer, and Governance, detailing actions for patients, clinicians, and AI systems with color-coded timelines for AI adoption, pilot, and future technologies.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Side-by-side dashboards visualize the maturity of AI applications in reproductive medicine. Panel A, an Evidence Maturity Dashboard, plots OCEBM evidence level against technology readiness, highlighting regions for \215Wait & Watch,\216 \215Pilot/Investigate,\216 and \215Adopt Now,\216 with colored dots representing different technologies based on readiness timelines. Panel B, an AI Maturity Map, plots clinical impact potential versus implementation readiness, similarly color-coding applications in \215Reassess,\216 \215High Impact/Low Readiness,\216 and \215Adopt Now\216 regions. Each technology \(e.g., outcome, embryo, sperm, ultrasound, RFID, stimulation, endometrial, miscarriage, robotic\) is labeled and placed according to its readiness and impact metrics.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating Mrs. K\220s Composite ARA Patient Journey for fertility treatment, divided into four phases: Pre-Treatment, Laboratory, Transfer & Risk, and Decision Re-evaluation. Each phase has specific milestones such as AI Outcome Prediction, Dose Optimization, Embryo Assessment, Ploidy Prediction, Miscarriage Risk Scoring, Revised Counseling, and Cascade Synthesis, with colored icons \(green, yellow, red\) indicating deployment readiness. Below each milestone, related clinical or AI-driven decision points are summarized. Color coding wave definitions are indicated at the bottom for clinical-deployment stages.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
